  "file": "staff-page.musa",
  "tokens": [
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A page of staff notation, read by an adapter and owned by a package." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `syntax staff { … }` is not ordinary Musa. The region's contents are read by" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the fixed lexer and grouper and handed to `std::adapters::staff`, which" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// answers with one ordinary expression — a call to `std::notation::staff`'s" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// `Document` constructor — that is then resolved, checked, and evaluated as if" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// it had been written out here. The adapter reads; the package decides." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Everything a musician states on a page is stated here: the instrument, how" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// far its written pitch sits from its sounding pitch, the clef, the key, the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// time it opens in, and how written values are to be spelled. Then the notation itself —" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// a pickup, a repeat with two endings, bars that each say what they measure," },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// notes, rests, chords, dots, exact durations, a tie across a bar line, a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// slur, a tuplet, a grace note, and a meter change." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Nothing is inherited. Every note states its own register and its own written" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// value, and every bar states its own length, so any one of them can be read" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// without reading the one before it — which is also what lets the adapter" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// report an unfull bar against the bar the composer wrote rather than against" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the page." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// # Why the score below is written out rather than realized from the page" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The page holds a grace note, and a grace note has no written span: when it" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// sounds is a performance question, and `std::notation::staff` refuses to" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// invent an answer to it. So `realize` refuses this page rather than placing" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// its grace somewhere, which is the deliberate silence rather than a fault." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A staff page becomes sound when a performance profile says how it is played;" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// until then it is notation, and the score below is the page's two repeated" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// bars written in the language the compiler reads today — the tie written as" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// its two halves, and `c5(3/8)` as the dotted quarter it is worth." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The head writes `time 4/4` and the bars write `bar (4, 4)`, which is one" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// signature spelled the two ways the adapter admits. A rational reaches an" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// adapter as the parts the lexer found, so `4/4` is a count of a unit here and" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// not the whole note it reduces to; `(4, 4)` says the same thing in the form" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// every other numbered word on the page uses." },
